<title>USA: Tribune sets two-for-one stock split.</title>
<headline>Tribune sets two-for-one stock split.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tribune Co said Wednesday its board had approved a two-for-one split of its common stock, payable January 15, record December 27.  </p>
<p>&quot;Tribune has great momentum and excellent prospects for the future, which have been reflected in the steady increase in our stock value,&quot; John Madigan, chairman, said in a statement. &quot;Tribune's cash flow should top $600 million this year.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787</p>
